  "maintainers": ["RadeenXALNW"],
  "units": "m",
  "description": "Interactive 3D figure for simple harmonic motion (সরল স্পন্দন গতি), book page 37, topic 2.2, next to চিত্র ২.০২ (দোলনা). A girl on a swing (or, as a second example, a 1 kg mass on a spring) oscillates about the equilibrium point (সাম্যবিন্দু): an orange arrow shows the speed, zero at the ends (প্রান্ত) and greatest at the equilibrium point, and blue dots on the path mark where it is every T/16, close together near the ends and far apart in the middle. The panel shows the speed in m/s and how it changes over one period (পর্যায়কাল). The student pulls the seat or the mass to one side and lets go (that sets the amplitude), pauses, steps, or slows time 4x. Physics: x = A cos ωt; swing L = 2 m, T = 2.84 s (small-swing formula, kept within 25°); spring k = 25 N/m, m = 1 kg, T = 1.26 s. Test tab: 5 questions (where the speed is greatest or zero, how it changes toward the equilibrium point, which journey takes one period, the period from a half-swing time, everyday examples). Phone-first, Bangla.",
